{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the equation of the tangent line to the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1aa12f384b6419f4ec067a7c8fc01fb6fff8c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3x^{2} - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> at the point (1,2)?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5b3aacb0f77b90074c1302869977923ed8d299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ y = x+1  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ y = 5x-3  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ y = 4x-2  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ y = 6x-4  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ y = 3x-1  \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"670\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb97999da4fc41cf798ca82b50b8b51b86a38fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39; = 6x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"19\" />, so at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, the slope of the tangent line at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500cf607cc9b677cdd752c5e325f281bbea5643f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 1 - 1 = 5 \\times 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The equation of the tangent line at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> must then be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390363ccf44cc4ef7df608c03948ea184c9ef35c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 5x - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercept. Plugging in our point, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3e74262bc7adcdc0c145d266e65c4bfe7bd99d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = 5 \\times 1 - b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34a4752ae06d95d4d34f4cc3c8ddb265189b423c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b + 5 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354e1b05fd5c5267dda823b8efb08b6a4d7f1e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 5 - 2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the equation of the tangent line at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96aec76801b07393c21b2c1fd7d85979176ee6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 5x - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can determine the slope of the tangent line at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Of the answer choices, the only one with a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96aec76801b07393c21b2c1fd7d85979176ee6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 5x - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2025 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Pro